 content="""
Refinement: Each PerRepoServerState already has a WorkerPool of Annex
objects.

When returning an Annex object to the pool, decide if it should be left
warmed up, or be cooled down (stopping helper processes etc).

To decide, have a quantity semaphore. Check it when getting an Annex
object from the WorkerPool. If there are too many warm objects, block
until one gets cooled down.

Question: PerRepoServerState also has an annexState and annexRead that are
not part of the AnnexWorkerPool so would not be affected by that. 
Are those used anywhere that spawns helper processes?
"""]]
